Description: Add a global SendHostname default to main.conf
 [IPv4].SendHostname can only be set per network, so a system that wants its
 hostname in every DHCP request has to add it to each profile. Add
 [Network].SendHostname to main.conf as the default, the same way
 [Network].EnableIPv6 is the default for [IPv6].Enabled. A profile's
 [IPv4].SendHostname still takes precedence. See docs/DECISIONS.md D21.
Author: dapalab <245609868+dapalab@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no (to be sent to iwd@lists.linux.dev)
Last-Update: 2026-09-30
---
diff --git a/src/iwd.config.rst b/src/iwd.config.rst
index b54670de..41a1a1ef 100644
--- a/src/iwd.config.rst
+++ b/src/iwd.config.rst
@@ -271,6 +271,13 @@ The group ``[Network]`` contains network configuration related settings.
 
        If not specified, ``300`` is used as default.
 
+   * - SendHostname
+     - Values: true, **false**
+
+       Sets the global default that tells **iwd** whether to include the
+       hostname in DHCP requests.  This setting is disabled by default.  This
+       setting can also be overridden on a per-network basis.
+
 Blacklist
 ---------
 
diff --git a/src/iwd.network.rst b/src/iwd.network.rst
index 892c6eb8..7a08a9d8 100644
--- a/src/iwd.network.rst
+++ b/src/iwd.network.rst
@@ -407,8 +407,9 @@ network configuration with the static addresses.
    * - SendHostname
      - Values: true, **false**
 
-       Configures DHCP to include the hostname in the request. This setting
-       is disabled by default.
+       Configures DHCP to include the hostname in the request. If not
+       specified, the ``[Network].SendHostname`` setting from main.conf is
+       used, which is disabled by default.
 
 The group ``[IPv6]`` contains settings for Internet Protocol version 6 (IPv6)
 network configuration.
